<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-meinhardt-echinoderm-pentaradial-symmetry> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Morris (2012), Mooi & David (1998/2008), Lovén (1874), Duboc et al. (2005), Luo & Su (2012) & Meinhardt (2008) echinoderm bilateral-to-pentaradial hydrocoel ring symmetry breaking with Ocular Plate Rule test growth (Strongylocentrotus purpuratus & Tripneustes gratilla (Echinoidea crown-group echinoderms))" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/meinhardt-echinoderm-pentaradial-symmetry-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/meinhardt-echinoderm-pentaradial-symmetry-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/meinhardt-echinoderm-pentaradial-symmetry-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/meinhardt-echinoderm-pentaradial-symmetry-4>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/meinhardt-echinoderm-pentaradial-symmetry-5> ;
    schema:about "Strongylocentrotus purpuratus & Tripneustes gratilla (Echinoidea crown-group echinoderms)" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: Quantitative reproduction of Duboc (2005) penetrance percentages or in-situ intensity profiles, mechanical plate packing, measured plate counts for any named species, or an integrated activator-inhibitor PDE in Section 2",
        "reconstructed_in_script: A circular-ring mode-selection solver with a prescribed dispersion curve, crescent-to-ring closure gates at the Lovén ray angles, an m in {3..7} circumference staircase and an equal-diffusion negative control; a 2D rudiment field with a binary Nodal switch; a reduced Ocular Plate Rule plate-addition solver on a spherical-cap test seeded from the ring lobes, with logistic plate accretion, ocular-end nucleation, Lovén-enlarged primordials and an aboral projection measured with the specimen's polar Fourier pipeline; a 1D steady-state screened-Poisson Nodal/BMP2-4 gradient model with Hill competence, a dose sweep and a 2D dose map; automated specimen segmentation of a Tripneustes gratilla test; 16 reference-anchored measurements; 5 Lean 4 theorems",
        "reported_in_source: Duboc et al. (2005): right-sided Nodal signalling represses the right hydrocoel; Nodal morpholino gives bilateral twin rudiments (2 x 5 podia) and bilateral Nodal overexpression gives none",
        "reported_in_source: Lovén (1874): in each ambulacrum one of the two primary peristomial plates is enlarged, in the asymmetric pattern Ib, IIb, IIIa, IVa, Va, and ambulacral/interambulacral plates form alternating biserial columns",
        "reported_in_source: Luo & Su (2012): BMP2/4 signalling on the left is required for rudiment formation and opposes Nodal",
        "reported_in_source: Meinhardt (2008): activator-inhibitor dynamics on a closed domain select a wavenumber set by domain circumference / critical wavelength",
        "reported_in_source: Mooi & David (1998, 2008): the Ocular Plate Rule — every new coronal plate is added at the ocular (apical) end of its column, so plate age increases toward the peristome and plate count increases with test size",
        "reported_in_source: Morris (2012): the pentaradial adult body plan arises from the left hydrocoel crescent closing into a ring, with the five primary podia initiated in the sequence II, IV, I, III, V (Carpenter C, A, D, B, E)",
        "reported_in_source: Raup (1968), Zachos (2009): echinoid test growth can be modelled as plate addition plus plate growth on a domed surface",
        "transfer_boundary: The Nodal/BMP2-4 gradient parameters were tuned only so that WT / MO / GOF give 5 / 10 / 0 podia; EC50 = 0.175 x WT is a model prediction with no empirical anchor; no Lefty/Pitx2 and no explicit Nodal-BMP antagonism term",
        "transfer_boundary: The OPR solver is 1D meridional plate heights in rectangular azimuth bands on a sphere: no plate-plate mechanics, Voronoi packing, FEM or ambitus flattening; growth factor 40, colatitudes 22/150 deg and h_nuc/h_max are labelled assumptions in the reference JSON; the Amb/IA plate ratio target 3.0 is approximate and the emergent value 2.06 misses it",
        "transfer_boundary: The Section 2 ring solver is NOT an integrated Gierer-Meinhardt PDE: the growth rate sigma(m) = 0.0480 (1 - 5.2 det^2) is hard-coded (L218, L283), the target mode is seeded in the initial condition (L289), the inhibitor is algebraic h = 1 + 0.65 (a - 1) (L318) and the Lovén initiation order is prescribed through delay_frac gates (L264-270). m* = 5, the staircase r = 1.0000 and the Lovén order r = 1.0000 therefore hold by construction; the DEFAULT_DA/DH/RHO constants (L120-123) do not enter the dynamics",
        "transfer_boundary: The specimen is Tripneustes gratilla while the header organism is S. purpuratus; specimen references (C_5 = 0.9255, ray angles) are the script's own segmentation outputs, not independent measurements" ;
    pk:anatomicalStructure "Biomineralized shell whorl / spicule / test in Strongylocentrotus purpuratus" ;
    pk:aristotelianEfficientCause "8. Crystal Accretion & TPMS" ;
    pk:aristotelianMegistonGenos "II. Anaima (Invertebrata)" ;
    pk:aristotelianPoionForm "Coiled Shells, Spicules & Gyroids" ;
    pk:aristotelianPosonLaw "Raup (W,D,S) / Gyroid Mean H=0" ;
    pk:aristotelianSubalternClass "Ostrakoderma (Mollusca & Echinodermata)" ;
    pk:biologicalGenus "Strongylocentrotus" ;
