<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-meinhardt-echinoderm-pentaradial-symmetry-code-traceability> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Morris (2012), Mooi & David (1998/2008), Lovén (1874), Duboc et al. (2005), Luo & Su (2012) & Meinhardt (2008) echinoderm bilateral-to-pentaradial hydrocoel ring symmetry breaking with Ocular Plate Rule test growth — Code-to-model traceability: 90/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Credited: the header docstring gained a Pass 3 block (L66-88) mapping Law 4 and Law 5 to their functions, sources and Lean theorems; every new function docstring names its source and Lean link (L565, L842); the math-KG YAML registers equations 4-5 with single-range code loci and re-pointed loci for equations 1-3; the measurement `method` strings explain each number. Deductions: the header title still reads \"Pass 2 (v2) Remediated Implementation\" (L3) (-1); the Section 2 docstrings and the README continue to describe the ring solver as a Gierer-Meinhardt PDE, which the code does not implement (L241-256) (-5); `render_comparison_figure`'s docstring still says \"6-panel Pass 2\" although it renders 9 panels (L972) (-1); the OPR GIF frame construction approximates history by rescaling final heights (L718-727) without saying so in the figure (-1)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-code-traceability> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/code-traceability" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "models/2005-meinhardt-echinoderm-pentaradial-symmetry.py L1–L4: Header title still 'Pass 2 (v2) Remediated Implementation' <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/a69596cc/models/2005-meinhardt-echinoderm-pentaradial-symmetry.py#L1-L4>",
        "models/2005-meinhardt-echinoderm-pentaradial-symmetry.py L241–L256: simulate_hydrocoel_ring_pde docstring presents a Gierer-Meinhardt crescent-to-ring PDE; the body is a templated mode solver <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/a69596cc/models/2005-meinhardt-echinoderm-pentaradial-symmetry.py#L241-L256>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-meinhardt-echinoderm-pentaradial-symmetry-code-traceability-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-meinhardt-echinoderm-pentaradial-symmetry-code-traceability-2> ;
    pk1:hasScore 9e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-meinhardt-echinoderm-pentaradial-symmetry-model-fidelity> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Morris (2012), Mooi & David (1998/2008), Lovén (1874), Duboc et al. (2005), Luo & Su (2012) & Meinhardt (2008) echinoderm bilateral-to-pentaradial hydrocoel ring symmetry breaking with Ocular Plate Rule test growth — Model fidelity to source: 86/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Credited: the OPR solver implements the mechanism Mooi & David describe — plates nucleate only at the ocular end (L627-631), existing plates grow logistically (L622-625), columns are biserial a/b with the Lovén-enlarged primordial seeding the zigzag (L520, L598-612), and the ring-PDE lobes genuinely set the ambulacral azimuths (L529-539, L580) so the two modules are coupled rather than juxtaposed; the enlargement ablation (phase 0.49 -> 0.00) is a real mechanistic test. The Nodal/BMP2-4 module is a proper steady-state reaction-diffusion reduction (screened Poisson with no-flux ends, L806-818; Hill competence, L821-823, L826-870) that reproduces Duboc's three phenotypes continuously and encodes Luo & Su's left-side BMP requirement. Deductions: the Section 2 ring solver is not a Gierer-Meinhardt integration — sigma(m) is a hard-coded parabola (L218, L283), the initial condition seeds the target mode (L289), the inhibitor is algebraic (L318) and the Lovén order is prescribed by delay_frac gates (L264-270, L305), so m* = 5 and both r = 1.0000 results are by construction and DEFAULT_DA/DH/RHO (L120-123) are unused in the dynamics (-9); the OPR test has no plate-plate mechanics, Voronoi packing or ambitus (-3); the Nodal model omits the Nodal-BMP antagonism of Luo & Su and Lefty/Pitx2, with Hill n = 4 arbitrary (-2); the 2D Panel D rudiment field (L468-512) still uses the binary Nodal switch and is not wired to the continuous model (-2); credit for two further Lean theorems (+2 net relative to the v2 basis)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "models/2005-meinhardt-echinoderm-pentaradial-symmetry.py L212–L218: compute_ring_dispersion: sigma(m) = 0.0480 (1 - 5.2 det^2) hard-coded; not derived from D_a, D_h, rho_a, rho_h <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/a69596cc/models/2005-meinhardt-echinoderm-pentaradial-symmetry.py#L212-L218>",
        "models/2005-meinhardt-echinoderm-pentaradial-symmetry.py L262–L270: Lovén initiation order prescribed through delay_frac gates at the Lovén angles, so the (II, IV, I, III, V) sequence r = 1.0000 is by construction <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/a69596cc/models/2005-meinhardt-echinoderm-pentaradial-symmetry.py#L262-L270>",
        "models/2005-meinhardt-echinoderm-pentaradial-symmetry.py L279–L292: simulate_hydrocoel_ring_pde: same hard-coded sigma_vec (L283) and the initial condition seeded with 0.025 cos(m* theta) at the TARGET mode (L289) <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/a69596cc/models/2005-meinhardt-echinoderm-pentaradial-symmetry.py#L279-L292>",
        "models/2005-meinhardt-echinoderm-pentaradial-symmetry.py L316–L318: Inhibitor is the algebraic relation h = 1 + 0.65 (a - 1), not an integrated PDE <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/a69596cc/models/2005-meinhardt-echinoderm-pentaradial-symmetry.py#L316-L318>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-meinhardt-echinoderm-pentaradial-symmetry-model-fidelity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-meinhardt-echinoderm-pentaradial-symmetry-model-fidelity-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-meinhardt-echinoderm-pentaradial-symmetry-model-fidelity-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-meinhardt-echinoderm-pentaradial-symmetry-model-fidelity-4> ;
    pk1:hasScore 8.6e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-meinhardt-echinoderm-pentaradial-symmetry-morphometric-validation> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Morris (2012), Mooi & David (1998/2008), Lovén (1874), Duboc et al. (2005), Luo & Su (2012) & Meinhardt (2008) echinoderm bilateral-to-pentaradial hydrocoel ring symmetry breaking with Ocular Plate Rule test growth — Morphometric validation: 88/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Credited: 16 reference-anchored measurements (9 from v2 + 7 new, L1576-1646), each with reference_value, unit, method and source; the Nodal dose-response deviation from Law 3 (0.055 podia) and the enlargement ablation are genuine model-vs-target tests; the alternation phase (0.49 vs 0.5) and Amb/IA ratio (2.06 vs ~3.0) are reported honestly including the miss. Deductions: `newest_at_ocular_fraction` = 1.0, the non-decreasing plate counts and Spearman rho = 0.9995 hold by construction of ocular-end nucleation (L627-631) — the method text says so (L1591) but they are counted as validations (-4); the alternation phase 0.49 follows from the chosen enlargement factor 1.5 (JSON), so its magnitude is semi-circular (-2); the aboral C_5 reference is the specimen's own value through the same pipeline and the specimen C_5 reference 0.9255 (L1735) is the script's own output (-3); the Nodal max |dev| is partly circular because K_N, K_B, lambda_N, lambda_B were tuned to the three targets, and EC50 has no empirical reference (-2); the Amb/IA reference 3.0 is unsourced (-1)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/morphometric-validation" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "datasets/echinoderm_pentaradial_symmetry/opr_plate_addition_nodal_dose_reference.json L60–L70: structural_reference_values: Amb/IA ratio 3.0 justified only as 'trigeminate compounding', not a measured count <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/a69596cc/datasets/echinoderm_pentaradial_symmetry/opr_plate_addition_nodal_dose_reference.json#L60-L70>",
        "models/2005-meinhardt-echinoderm-pentaradial-symmetry.py L1586–L1592: newest-at-ocular measurement whose method text concedes it 'holds by construction of ocular-end nucleation' <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/a69596cc/models/2005-meinhardt-echinoderm-pentaradial-symmetry.py#L1586-L1592>",
        "models/2005-meinhardt-echinoderm-pentaradial-symmetry.py L1733–L1740: Specimen C_5 reference_value 0.9255 is the script's own segmentation output (self-referential) <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/a69596cc/models/2005-meinhardt-echinoderm-pentaradial-symmetry.py#L1733-L1740>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-meinhardt-echinoderm-pentaradial-symmetry-measurement-canonical-hydrocoel-ring-primary-podia-mode-m-at-r-ring-75-um>,
