<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-meinhardt-echinoderm-pentaradial-symmetry-specimen-match> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Morris (2012), Mooi & David (1998/2008), Lovén (1874), Duboc et al. (2005), Luo & Su (2012) & Meinhardt (2008) echinoderm bilateral-to-pentaradial hydrocoel ring symmetry breaking with Ocular Plate Rule test growth — Morphological realism / specimen match: 89/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Credited: the Tripneustes gratilla test segmentation (L916-962) is unchanged and now shares a single polar chromaticity + azimuthal FFT pipeline (`polar_c5_harmonics`, L759-800) with the synthetic OPR test projection (L739-756), so the specimen and the model are measured identically; the specimen's ambulacral duty cycle (0.575) calibrates the synthetic ambulacral width; the 9-panel comparison figure places the specimen (Panel E), its spectrum (Panel F) and the plated dome / harmonics inset (Panels G, I) side by side; the OPR figure insets both images. Deductions: a synthetic exactly five-fold test has C_5 ~ 1 regardless of plate kinetics, so the 0.9964 vs 0.9255 comparison discriminates nothing about the accretion model (-4); detected synthetic ray angles [7, 80, 138, 210, 281] are noisy because the synthetic profile has flat tops (-2); the species mismatch (header organism S. purpuratus, specimen and \"trigeminate\" argument T. gratilla) persists (-3); no plate-level comparison (plate counts per column, plate outlines) is made against the specimen, which is the morphology the new solver actually produces (-3)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-specimen-match> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/specimen-match" ;
